# Rule Quality Checklist

Use this checklist when editing root agent instructions or generated workflow docs.

- Root instructions stay under roughly 150-200 lines.
- Rules are specific and actionable.
- Long procedures live in docs or skills, not root instructions.
- Verification commands are real, or explicitly marked not configured.
- Local-only files and secrets are ignored by Git.
- Rules do not conflict with each other.
- Existing user changes are not overwritten by default.
- Commits are not created without explicit approval.
- Unsupported adapters stay out of scope unless the plan is amended.

